{
  "reviewer": "abstract_conclusion_consistency_auditor",
  "paper_id": "bicycle-infrastructure-paper",
  "run_status": "ok",
  "summary": "The abstract, introduction and conclusion were compared with the body. Most headline counts match the body (70/34/2 pilot funnel, 97% agreement, 3,187/92/43/29, 14 of 15 counties, 700 579 listings, 38%). I found ten consistency problems. The abstract says the data are linked to housing listings, but the body says no linkage has been done. The summaries carry the three-positive pilot agreement result, the unvalidated full-run counts, and the one-case NVDB illustration with less qualification than the body, which says the agreement result is 'indicative only' and lists unvalidated and manual steps as next steps. The summaries omit the body's finding that date precision depends on media attention. The abstract's 'only two actual openings' conflicts with the Table 2 footnote that Grettefoss opened on 3 November. Section 3.1.2 reports '2 of 34 articles' where Section 3.1.4 reports five relevant articles. Footnote 3 contradicts Section 4.1 on how the Stord article was coded. Parser quality was acceptable for the page text used. All quotes come from the per-page text files, not the structured table files.",
  "findings": [
    {
